  (:adr/decision-summary
  (map (:finding
   (map (:claim "orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-ind-clean-air existed on disk as a local-only scaffold (blueprint.edn, deps.edn, src/clean_air/portfolio.cljc, one 3-assertion test) with no .git directory, no GitHub repo, and no manifest/west.yml or manifest/repos.edn entry — a west-orphan.")
    (:evidence "A prior read-only audit found the existing code (eligible?/priority-score/select-portfolio pure functions, evidence-gated + council-approval-gated India air-quality intervention portfolio selection) real and correctly matching its stated purpose, but thin/incomplete relative to fleet conventions: no independent verification layer, no regulatory citations, no doc set, and only 3 test assertions.")
    (:owner-approval "Owner explicitly approved completion and registration (\"登録して完成\").")))
   (:architecture-decision
   (map (:choice "A three-namespace pure decision LAYER (clean-air.regulatory / clean-air.registry / clean-air.governor) behind the original clean-air.portfolio ranking functions -- NOT a langgraph-clj StateGraph actor (Advisor|-Governor + phase + audit-ledger-store) like cloud-itonami-hygiene-access or cloud-itonami-iso3166-ind.")
    (:why "This domain has no LLM advisor proposing interventions -- candidates arrive from a human NCAP city/state action-plan process -- and blueprint.edn's own :itonami.blueprint/non-goals explicitly excludes :autonomous-enforcement and :autonomous-subsidy-disbursement. Standing up the full Advisor|-Governor StateGraph pattern other cloud-itonami actors need to contain an LLM's self-report would be a bigger pattern than this domain requires. What the domain DOES require -- and what the original scaffold was missing -- is independent verification: the original eligible? trusted a candidate map's own inline :evidence/:approval keys, which a caller could set without any real dossier or vote ever happening. This build fixes that by requiring the SAME ground-truth-not-self-report discipline every other cloud-itonami actor's own registry establishes (e.g. hygaccess.registry), implemented as pure functions over two independently-supplied ledgers rather than a StateGraph.")))
   (:governance-hardening
   (map (:mechanism "clean-air.governor/decide returns :hold (HARD, evidence or approval independently fails against the ledger) / :escalate (SOFT, independently verified but a narrow approval-vote-margin or single-source-evidence signal is present) / :commit (independently clean, eligible for the ranked portfolio).")
    (:ledgers "clean-air.registry/evidence-complete? and council-approved? consult caller-supplied evidence-ledger/approval-ledger vectors (append-only record maps) keyed by intervention id -- never a candidate's own :evidence/:approval flags, which clean-air.portfolio's candidate maps no longer even carry.")
    (:closed-sets "clean-air.regulatory/recognized-evidence-authorities (#{:cpcb :state-pollution-control-board :moefcc :ncap-prana :caqm :who :peer-reviewed-study :academic-institution}) and recognized-approval-bodies (modeled on NCAP's real city-level review committee -> district-level committee -> state-level Steering Committee -> national MoEF&CC-Secretary-chaired NCAP steering committee with CPCB Chairman sign-off chain) are the closed sets an evidence/approval record must be independently originated by to count.")))
   (:regulatory-grounding
   (map (:naaqs "CPCB National Ambient Air Quality Standards, notified 2009: PM2.5 annual 40 ug/m3 / 24-hr 60 ug/m3; PM10 annual 60 ug/m3 / 24-hr 100 ug/m3 (plus SO2/NO2/CO/O3/NH3/Pb). Source: https://cpcb.nic.in/air-quality-standard/ (read via mirror https://www.apsed.in/post/naaqs-india-cpcb-ambient-air-quality-standards-all-pollutants after cpcb.nic.in was unreachable at fetch time; cross-checked against the NAAQS 2009 PDF mirrors at scclmines.com and hppcb.nic.in, all three agree).")
    (:who-aqg "WHO 2021 Global Air Quality Guidelines: PM2.5 annual AQG 5 ug/m3 (down from 10 in 2005) with four stepwise Interim Targets (35/25/15/10 ug/m3); PM10 annual AQG 15 ug/m3 (down from 20). Source: https://www.who.int/news-room/questions-and-answers/item/who-global-air-quality-guidelines")
    (:ncap "National Clean Air Programme, launched January 2019 (MoEF&CC), ~130 non-attainment/million-plus cities across 24 states/UTs, target revised to up to 40% PM10 reduction OR meeting the PM10 NAAQS (60 ug/m3) by FY2025-26 (from an original 20-30% by FY2024-25 vs a 2017-18 baseline), funded via NCAP + XV Finance Commission grants, tracked via the PRANA portal. Per the CREA 'Tracing the Hazy Air 2026' progress report: only 23 of 130 covered cities have met the revised target and 190 of 229 monitored cities nationwide still exceed the PM10 NAAQS -- a documented, ongoing gap. Sources: https://energyandcleanair.org/publication/2026-progress-report-on-national-clean-air-programme/ , https://prana.cpcb.gov.in/")
    (:discipline "Every regulatory number cites a source actually fetched and read during this build; nothing was fabricated. Illustrative intervention/ledger examples in test/clean_air/fixtures.clj (household counts, meeting ids) are explicitly marked synthetic test data, not claims about a real currently-approved grant.")))
   (:doc-and-template-convention
   (map (:doc-set "README.md, LICENSE (AGPL-3.0-or-later, copied verbatim from sibling repos), GOVERNANCE.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md, SECURITY.md, .gitignore -- house style adapted from cloud-itonami-iso3166-ind/-egy (doc-file shape, deps.edn cognitect-test-runner + clj-kondo alias convention) and cloud-itonami-hygiene-access (Governor/ground-truth-not-self-report prose discipline, scaled down to match this domain's actual decision-LAYER shape rather than copying its full manufacturing-actor architecture).")
    (:blueprint-completion "blueprint.edn completed with :itonami.blueprint/license, :governor (:clean-air-portfolio-governor), :robotics false, :status :public-oss (was :pilot, which is not a value the fleet's :itonami.blueprint/status field actually uses -- surveyed 1115 blueprint.edn files, :public-oss is used in 837/837 non-blob entries), :maturity :implemented, and :implemented-slice summarizing the architecture. No organization.edn was added -- surveyed cloud-itonami-hygiene-access (a thematic, non-country-level repo like this one) and confirmed organization.edn is specific to country-level iso3166-* repos representing a government entity itself, not thematic sub-repos.")))
   (:test-coverage
   (map (:before "1 deftest, 3 assertions (happy path + approval-gate + evidence-gate) trusting inline candidate flags.")
    (:after "61 tests / 114 assertions across clean_air.regulatory-test, clean_air.registry-test, clean_air.governor-test, clean_air.portfolio-test -- covering the hold/escalate/commit decision space (including both-reasons-present, hold-priority-over-approval-when-both-fail), every ledger-verification predicate (valid-evidence-record?/evidence-complete?/majority-quorum-approval?/council-approved?/narrow-margin?/single-source-evidence?) with both accept and reject cases, priority-score weight math, portfolio ranking/filtering/tie-breaking, and regulatory-fact sanity checks. clj-kondo: 0 errors, 0 warnings. The original 3-assertion test is kept verbatim (ported to the new ledger-based API) as council-approval-and-evidence-are-both-required so the original intent stays traceable.")))
   (:verification
   (map (:tests "clojure -M:test => Ran 61 tests containing 114 assertions. 0 failures, 0 errors.")
    (:lint "clojure -M:lint => linting took ~300ms, errors: 0, warnings: 0.")
    (:github "gh repo create cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-ind-clean-air --public; confirmed visibility PUBLIC, default branch main, pushed commit eccd120dcfb33e5c107d6f36b1e19a7b8751ba4a matches https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-ind-clean-air")
    (:manifest "manifest/repos.edn :manifest.repos/extra-projects gained one entry (orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-ind-clean-air) via a proper EDN read -> conj -> pr-str write (not manual string surgery); nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --entry cloud-itonami-iso3166-ind-clean-air produced a minimal 5-line west.yml diff (correct alphabetical position between cloud-itonami-iso3166-ind and cloud-itonami-iso3166-irl) and passed server-side pin verification against GitHub (pin eccd120dcfb3 reachable from cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-ind-clean-air's default branch main). nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --check reports the OVERALL west.yml STALE, but this reflects pre-existing, unrelated pin drift from concurrent sessions across the fleet (matching the precedent documented in ADR-2607177500) -- not this registration's own entry, which was individually --entry-verified; a wholesale regeneration was correctly NOT performed (CLAUDE.md / ADR-2607022900 forbid it).")
    (:worktree-isolation "The superproject's own shared main checkout showed active concurrent-session writes to manifest/repos.edn and manifest/west.yml mid-task (observed, then found already reverted/committed by that session moments later) -- per CLAUDE.md's worktree-per-agent convention, all manifest/ADR editing for THIS task was done in an isolated sibling git worktree (outside the superproject root) on branch registration/cloud-itonami-iso3166-ind-clean-air, landed via a feature-branch push + server-side merge (gh api .../merges), never by editing/committing directly in the shared checkout. A pre-existing uncommitted west.yml pin-advance (unrelated repos: cloud-itonami-iso3166-usa-hhs/-sba, toshokan) found in the shared checkout was preserved via git stash (not dropped) rather than discarded.")))))
  (:adr/body
  "# ADR-2607199980: cloud-itonami-iso3166-ind-clean-air — orphaned local scaffold completed and registered\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-19\n\n## Context\n\nA local-only scaffold existed at `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-ind-clean-air/` — `blueprint.edn`, `deps.edn`, `src/clean_air/portfolio.cljc`, one 3-assertion test — with no `.git` directory, no GitHub repository, and no `manifest/west.yml`/`manifest/repos.edn` entry: a west-orphan. It is a THEMATIC sub-repo of the India (`iso3166-ind`) family, covering air-quality-intervention-portfolio-selection under the National Clean Air Programme (NCAP) domain. A prior read-only audit found the existing code real and correctly matching its stated purpose (evidence-gated, council-approval-gated portfolio selection over pure `eligible?`/`priority-score`/`select-portfolio` functions), but thin relative to fleet conventions: no independent verification of the evidence/approval it gated on, no regulatory citations, no doc set. The owner explicitly approved completion and registration (\"登録して完成\").\n\n## Decision\n\n### 1. Architecture: a pure decision LAYER, not a langgraph-clj StateGraph actor\n\nUnlike `cloud-itonami-hygiene-access` or `cloud-itonami-iso3166-ind` (both Advisor⊣Governor StateGraph actors with an LLM advisor, phase rollout, and an append-only audit-ledger store), this domain has **no LLM advisor** — candidate interventions arrive from a human NCAP city/state action-plan process, not from this actor. `blueprint.edn`'s own `:itonami.blueprint/non-goals` explicitly excludes `:autonomous-enforcement` and `:autonomous-subsidy-disbursement`. Standing up the full StateGraph + phase + store machinery other cloud-itonami actors need to contain an LLM's self-report would be a bigger pattern than this domain requires — so this build kept the original scaffold's pure-function shape (`clean-air.portfolio`) rather than architecturally upgrading it to a StateGraph actor.\n\n### 2. The actual hardening: ledger-backed independent verification\n\nWhat the domain genuinely needed — and what the original scaffold was missing — is **independent verification**. The original `eligible?` trusted a candidate map's own inline `:evidence #{...}`/`:approval :approved-by-council` keys; nothing stopped a caller from writing those keys with no real dossier or council vote behind them. This build adds two new namespaces:\n\n- **`clean-air.regulatory`** — citation-grounded India air-quality facts (CPCB NAAQS 2009, WHO 2021 Global Air Quality Guidelines, NCAP institutional facts and progress) plus two CLOSED sets: `recognized-evidence-authorities` (`#{:cpcb :state-pollution-control-board :moefcc :ncap-prana :caqm :who :peer-reviewed-study :academic-institution}`) and `recognized-approval-bodies`, the latter modeled on NCAP's real approval chain (city-level review committee → district-level committee → state-level Steering Committee → national MoEF&CC-Secretary-chaired NCAP steering committee with CPCB Chairman sign-off).\n- **`clean-air.registry`** — `evidence-complete?`/`council-approved?` verify a caller-supplied evidence-ledger/approval-ledger (append-only record-map vectors) by intervention id, never a candidate's own flags; plus `narrow-margin?` (a one-vote approval margin) and `single-source-evidence?` (every evidence record from the same body, no independent corroboration) as SOFT escalation signals.\n- **`clean-air.governor`** — `decide` composes these into `:hold` (HARD)/`:escalate` (SOFT)/`:commit`, mirroring the fleet's own HARD/SOFT vocabulary (e.g. `hygaccess.governor`'s confidence/high-stakes gate) without needing that actor's full machinery.\n\n`clean-air.portfolio`'s candidate maps no longer carry `:evidence`/`:approval` fields at all — `select-portfolio` takes the candidate list AND the two ledgers as separate arguments, structurally preventing a caller from fabricating eligibility inline.\n\n### 3. Regulatory grounding (verified via web search, cited in each var's docstring)\n\n- **CPCB NAAQS (2009)**: PM2.5 annual 40 µg/m³ / 24-hr 60 µg/m³; PM10 annual 60 µg/m³ / 24-hr 100 µg/m³. https://cpcb.nic.in/air-quality-standard/\n- **WHO 2021 Global Air Quality Guidelines**: PM2.5 annual AQG 5 µg/m³ (IT-1..IT-4: 35/25/15/10); PM10 annual AQG 15 µg/m³. https://www.who.int/news-room/questions-and-answers/item/who-global-air-quality-guidelines\n- **NCAP**: launched Jan 2019, ~130 cities/24 states-UTs, target revised to ≤40% PM10 reduction or NAAQS by FY2025-26; per CREA's 'Tracing the Hazy Air 2026' report only 23/130 cities met the revised target and 190/229 monitored cities still exceed PM10 NAAQS. https://energyandcleanair.org/publication/2026-progress-report-on-national-clean-air-programme/ , https://prana.cpcb.gov.in/\n\nAn initial web-search auto-summary for the CPCB PM2.5/PM10 limits returned numbers matching WHO's 2021 guideline instead of CPCB's actual NAAQS — caught by cross-checking against three independent mirrors of the NAAQS 2009 PDF before using the figures anywhere. No domain fact in this build was used without such verification.\n\n### 4. Doc-set and template convention\n\n`README.md`/`GOVERNANCE.md`/`CONTRIBUTING.md`/`CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md`/`SECURITY.md`/`LICENSE` (AGPL-3.0-or-later) follow `cloud-itonami-iso3166-ind`/`-egy`'s doc-file shape and `deps.edn` alias convention (cognitect test-runner + clj-kondo), with prose discipline (Governor independence, ground-truth-not-self-report) adapted from `cloud-itonami-hygiene-access` — scaled to this repo's actual decision-LAYER shape, not copying that repo's full manufacturing-actor architecture. `blueprint.edn` was completed with `:license`, `:governor :clean-air-portfolio-governor`, `:robotics false`, `:status :public-oss` (corrected from `:pilot`, not a value the fleet's `:itonami.blueprint/status` field uses anywhere in a 1115-file survey), `:maturity :implemented`, and an `:implemented-slice` summary. No `organization.edn` was added: that file is specific to country-level `iso3166-*` repos representing a government entity, and this is a thematic sub-repo (confirmed by `cloud-itonami-hygiene-access`, a comparable thematic repo, also lacking one).\n\n### 5. Test coverage: 3 assertions → 61 tests / 114 assertions\n\nNew `test/clean_air/{regulatory,registry,governor,portfolio}_test.clj` plus a shared `test/clean_air/fixtures.clj` (synthetic/illustrative ledger data, explicitly documented as such — not a claim about any real currently-approved NCAP grant) cover every hold/escalate/commit path, every ledger-verification predicate's accept/reject cases, priority-score math, portfolio ranking/filtering/tie-breaking, and regulatory-fact sanity checks. The original 3-assertion test is kept verbatim (ported to the new ledger-based API) as `council-approval-and-evidence-are-both-required`.\n\n## Consequences\n\n(+) This repo now has real, independently-verifiable governance rigor matching the fleet's actual safety bar (ground-truth-not-self-report), without carrying a StateGraph actor's weight the domain does not need.\n\n(+) Every regulatory number is citation-grounded and traceable to a source actually fetched and read.\n\n(+) The doc set, blueprint.edn shape, and deps.edn alias convention match sibling `iso3166-*` repos, so this repo reads as a native fleet member rather than a one-off.\n\n(-) `nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --check` reports the overall `west.yml` STALE due to pre-existing, unrelated concurrent-session pin drift across the fleet (not this registration's own entry) — matching the same documented condition in ADR-2607177500; per CLAUDE.md/ADR-2607022900 a wholesale regeneration was correctly not performed to fix this.\n\n(-) The superproject's shared main checkout showed a concurrent session actively writing to `manifest/repos.edn`/`manifest/west.yml` mid-task; this registration's own edits were made in an isolated sibling worktree and landed via feature-branch + server-side merge specifically to avoid colliding with that WIP, per CLAUDE.md's worktree-per-agent convention.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `clojure -M:test` → 61 tests / 114 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n- `clojure -M:lint` → 0 errors, 0 warnings.\n- GitHub: https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-ind-clean-air (public, default branch `main`, initial commit `eccd120dcfb33e5c107d6f36b1e19a7b8751ba4a`).\n- `manifest/repos.edn` `:extra-projects` gained one entry via a proper EDN read→conj→pr-str write; `nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --entry cloud-itonami-iso3166-ind-clean-air` produced a 5-line `west.yml` diff and passed server-side pin verification (GitHub API, pin reachable from `main`).\n- `nbb scripts/west-orphan-audit.cljs --blocking` re-run after landing to confirm this repo no longer appears in the orphan list (see follow-up commit/session note if this exit code is non-zero for unrelated reasons, per the same caveat pattern as ADR-2607177500).")))
